Now that the tournament's over, I'm interested to read any kind of
spoilers about the Pacman challenge.  Here are my observations:

I found the fruit-eating trigger/restriction to be a sensible midpoint
between Elbereth in the KoL challenge (which some players didn't find at
all due to never using it) and darkness in the Grue challenge (which
caused a lot of frustration, especially when resulting from engulfing
attacks).  Though I don't understand why carrots were included.

Once the inverted-strcmp-logic bug was fixed, I took a couple of
attempts to complete the challenge.  I beat it as a Ranger, by finding
the portal (thanks to automatic searching) then coming back with speed,
a beartrap and a couple of wands of teleport. 

I picked up all the pellets and fruit tokens but couldn't work out how
to use them.  I'd have assumed that it would be possible to destroy the
ghosts (maybe only temporarily) with the use of the pellets, but I
couldn't (e)at, (a)pply or #invoke them, and wielding or throwing them
gave no suggestion that they were doing incredible amounts of damage to
the ghosts.  Did anyone have any luck here?

I considered destroying the ghosts the traditional way, but a
stethoscope (or possibly a wand of probing) showed me that they had lots
of HP and a respectable AC, I didn't have impressive firepower, and
meleeing them uses up lives quickly.

The ghosts weren't caught by the beartrap on the floor, although
randomly generated monsters caught in the trap would provide a barrier.

When stuck in a corner, zapping a /oTele at the approaching ghost was a
good escape plan (and thankfully didn't move the lit squares to random
positions around the level).  One of the ghosts landed in the space
above the maze, which kept it out of the way permanently.


